---
import Polaroid from './Polaroid.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---
<section class="about-scrapbook section-pad" aria-labelledby="about-intro"><span class="margin-note hand">about me!</span><div class="about-collage reveal"><Polaroid src="images/rayandika.webp" alt="Muhammad Rayandika smiling" caption="yep, that's me :)" class="portrait-note" /><div class="about-intro"><h2 id="about-intro" class="outlined-label">what's up</h2><p class="hand">I'm an AI Agent Engineer with 4+ years in software engineering. <span aria-hidden="true">✧</span> I build intelligent agent teams that collaborate, connect with your business tools, and take repetitive work off your plate. Thoughtful interfaces and reliable software are still at the heart of everything I build.</p><div class="skill-stickers" aria-label="Areas of focus"><span class="torn yellow">Multi-Agent Systems</span><span class="torn yellow mini" aria-hidden="true">✦</span><span class="torn green">Agent Workflows</span><span class="torn green mini" aria-hidden="true">⌘</span><span class="torn pink">Workflow Automation</span><span class="torn pink mini" aria-hidden="true">✳</span><span class="torn blue">Software Engineering</span><span class="torn blue mini" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div><a class="ink-link about-more" href={`${base}/about/`}>A little more about me ↗</a></div><Polaroid src="images/scrapbook/setup.webp" alt="My desk in Bandung: a Lenovo monitor with a terminal open, a MacBook beside it, and a cream-and-orange mechanical keyboard on a desk mat" caption="where the agents get built" class="studio-note" /></div></section>
